  "texts": {
    "preamble": "(Krishna Agrotech Limited & Anr vs Union Of India on 7 September, 2015 Author: Dipankar Datta Bench: Dipankar Datta 1 178 07.09.2015 rrc W. P. 21434 (W) of 2015 (Krishna Agrotech Limited & Anr. Vs. Union of India & Ors.) Mr. Rajesh Upadhyay .....For the petitioners Mr. Subhadip Roy ......For the respdt. nos. 2 to 6 Mr. Sabyasachi Chowdhury Ms. Sanchari Chakraborty ......For the respdt. nos. 7 & 8",
    "facts": "Contracts were entered into by and between the petitioners for purchase of biscuits from the said respondents 7 & 8, pursuant whereto the biscuits purchased by the petitioners were exported to Sierra Leone, West Africa. According to the petitioners, the cartons of biscuits exported by them upon testing by the Government of Sierra Leone, Ministry of Health & Sanitation, Environmental Health Division were found to contain biscuits that had expired long back and, thus, unfit for human consumption. This writ petition dated 24th August, 2015 has been presented by the petitioners seeking a direction on the official respondents (officials of the Food, Safety & Standards Authority of India) to enforce the provisions of the Food, Safety & Standards Act, 2006 by initiating prosecution against the respondents 7 & 8. In my view, the petitioners have presented this writ petition for oblique motives and it is not a bona fide litigation. If at all the respondents 7 & 8 had passed off expired biscuits, it was the duty of the petitioners to have made appropriate inspection before purchasing the same. Their claim sounds in damages.",
    "arguments": "",
